#X obj 659 8 array.play~;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 166 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 The object plays back the specified array with variable
speed \, amplitude and interpolation. Playback can be started with
a bang (from the beginning) or with a float (from the given sample
position). Negative float offsets are counted from the end of the array.
The playback range can be limited with @begin and @end \, and the object
can output the current play position periodically (see @clock and @cfmt).
Playback can also be looped or paused.;
